    "note": "STAMP reports a separate benchmark level for each skill and does not publish an A1 pass/fail decision. Coding Adventures maps A1 to ILR 0+ in core/exam-levels.json; Avant's Arabic technical report maps ILR 0+ to Level 3 / Novice-High. The project therefore requires Level 3 in every skill: 3/9 for reading and listening and 3/8 for writing and speaking. maximumPoints and passPoints use the receptive scale only because this schema requires one headline pair; the four independent ratios encode the real project floor. This is not an Avant pass rule, no composite average may hide a lower skill, and the target is Modern Standard Arabic rather than a dialect claim."
